WEBVTT

00:28.420 --> 00:30.090
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

00:31.470 --> 00:36.770
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

01:30.610 --> 01:35.490
PLAYER.07: SUNSTEAL SCRAMBLE

01:36.410 --> 01:40.500
Excellent! I didn't know
such a rare game existed!

01:40.500 --> 01:43.570
Oh, you've got fine taste, young lady.

01:44.470 --> 01:47.600
But that's a legendary board game.

01:47.600 --> 01:50.840
It's quite pricey for your pocket money.

01:52.460 --> 01:54.570
I've got plenty of money in my pocket.

01:55.970 --> 01:57.280
I'll use this card!

02:00.600 --> 02:02.080
T-This card...!

02:02.080 --> 02:05.690
A platinum credit card
with unlimited usage!

02:05.690 --> 02:10.050
Can you ship all the games
from this store to Ruin?

02:10.050 --> 02:12.750
Y-Yes! I'll arrange it right away!

02:12.750 --> 02:13.970
Thank you!

02:15.970 --> 02:17.380
Hey, Leshea.

02:18.500 --> 02:21.790
Chief Secretary Miranda told you
not to use it too much, right?

02:22.300 --> 02:25.980
Yeah. I'll buy up a couple more stores,
and then I'll be done.

02:31.840 --> 02:34.260
And you bought a lot of snacks too...

02:34.260 --> 02:35.490
Yes.

02:36.540 --> 02:41.250
It's my reward for overcoming
that intense battle yesterday.

02:46.910 --> 02:48.900
So let's go!

02:48.900 --> 02:49.960
To where?

02:49.960 --> 02:52.080
There's a famous takoyaki
restaurant near here!

02:52.080 --> 02:53.360
Are you still going to eat?!

02:53.360 --> 02:54.580
Of course!

02:54.580 --> 02:55.220
- That's the famous restaurant after all!

02:55.220 --> 02:56.970
- Umm... Lady Dragon God!
- That's the famous restaurant after all!

02:56.970 --> 02:58.370
- Umm... Lady Dragon God!
- Hmm?

02:58.370 --> 03:00.330
Please take a picture with us!

03:00.330 --> 03:02.590
Huh? Me?

03:03.250 --> 03:05.490
And your autograph too!

03:06.790 --> 03:10.100
Has this ever happened
to Leshea before?

03:10.100 --> 03:12.810
People in Ruin are pretty afraid of her...

03:13.610 --> 03:14.630
I see.

03:15.060 --> 03:19.370
If they didn't know how dangerous she was,
she would be very cute.

03:20.250 --> 03:22.650
She's a bit confused, though.

03:22.650 --> 03:24.450
E-Excuse me!

03:25.060 --> 03:27.570
We were watching the game yesterday!

03:27.570 --> 03:31.180
Fay, Your gameplay was cool,
and I would love to get your autograph!

03:31.180 --> 03:33.190
Can I also ask you
to shake hands with me?

03:33.190 --> 03:35.300
P-Please wait...

03:38.020 --> 03:41.660
No way! I don't even get
this kind of treatment in Ruin!

03:41.660 --> 03:45.610
I-Is this what it means to be a guest
on the World Games Tour?!

03:45.610 --> 03:50.050
That means I,
the real star of yesterday,

03:50.050 --> 03:53.510
will have people wait in line
for my autographs,

03:53.510 --> 03:55.790
just like at a popular theme park attraction!

03:55.790 --> 03:59.140
Now, come on! O fans of mine!

04:04.970 --> 04:08.810
I'm going to buy some crepe...

04:12.720 --> 04:14.300
Thank you very much!

04:17.370 --> 04:19.030
It's finally over...

04:19.770 --> 04:21.430
I was so nervous.

04:21.430 --> 04:24.090
Well, I wasn't used to this treatment,

04:24.090 --> 04:27.630
and I haven't signed anything
since six months ago.

04:29.030 --> 04:30.960
I want your autograph!

04:30.960 --> 04:31.850
Huh?

04:31.850 --> 04:33.840
What are you going to do with that?

04:33.840 --> 04:35.870
I'll keep it as a treasure!

04:35.870 --> 04:38.090
Isn't that human culture, right?

04:38.090 --> 04:38.990
Well...

04:38.990 --> 04:41.460
Give me! As proof of our friendship!

04:42.560 --> 04:45.180
Okay. Then, where's your autograph pad?

04:45.180 --> 04:46.180
I don't have it.

04:46.180 --> 04:49.270
Then maybe we can stop by the stationery
store on the way home...

04:57.830 --> 04:59.030
I want it now.

04:59.520 --> 05:01.870
I mean, you don't have...

05:01.870 --> 05:06.080
It doesn't have to be an autograph pad.
I wouldn't mind if it was right on my skin.

05:06.900 --> 05:09.040
You can sign on the back of my ribbon.

05:09.040 --> 05:12.080
I don't know if I can sign
on the back of the ribbon.

05:12.080 --> 05:15.670
Because it feels more like
"this only belongs to me."

05:23.820 --> 05:25.340
Okay. There you have it.

05:27.230 --> 05:30.560
Hooray! I'll treasure this!

05:35.020 --> 05:37.590
What are you two doing?

05:37.590 --> 05:38.640
Woah!

05:38.640 --> 05:41.460
You were standing weirdly
close to each other.

05:42.390 --> 05:45.700
No, it's just that Leshea asked me
for my autograph.

05:46.990 --> 05:48.720
I'm not lying!

05:49.490 --> 05:50.450
What's your problem?!

05:53.940 --> 05:55.170
Ah!

05:59.350 --> 06:01.090
What's with that crowd over there?

06:01.090 --> 06:02.690
Master Dax!

06:02.690 --> 06:04.550
Master Dax, please look this way!

06:04.550 --> 06:06.020
Dax?

06:06.020 --> 06:09.810
Could it be that's...
They're filming "Dax Lunch"!

06:09.810 --> 06:11.110
What's that?

06:11.110 --> 06:14.110
It's a broadcast of him eating his lunch!

06:14.110 --> 06:15.230
That's it?!

06:15.230 --> 06:18.770
Tens of thousands of his fans
watch him eat in real time.

06:18.770 --> 06:21.320
Rumor has it that broadcast alone
brings in twice

06:21.320 --> 06:23.680
as much money as an apostle's salary!

06:23.680 --> 06:25.670
That's completely insane!

06:25.670 --> 06:27.410
He's a popular guy, after all.

06:29.900 --> 06:32.540
Umm... Kelritch?

06:32.990 --> 06:34.830
Thank you for the game yesterday.

06:35.410 --> 06:38.190
He's a top-notch game player
with a clear mind,

06:38.190 --> 06:40.060
an excellent athlete, handsome,

06:40.590 --> 06:43.740
tall, and friendly.

06:43.740 --> 06:45.590
How could he not be popular?

06:45.590 --> 06:47.060
Look who's got a honey tongue...

06:47.060 --> 06:48.410
I'm just telling you the truth.

06:48.410 --> 06:51.660
Are you going to be in
"Dax Lunch" too, Kelritch?

06:51.660 --> 06:56.170
No, of course not.
To me, Dax is just a business partner.

06:56.170 --> 06:59.270
I am not involved in his
personal life away from the team,

06:59.270 --> 07:01.690
nor do I have any feelings for him.

07:01.690 --> 07:03.430
O-Okay...

07:03.430 --> 07:05.410
Well then, have a good day.

07:07.950 --> 07:10.930
But she's walking toward
the filming location.

07:12.610 --> 07:15.500
All the apostles in this city
have their quirks, don't they?

07:16.220 --> 07:17.960
Don't you think so?

07:17.960 --> 07:18.950
Nel.

07:19.810 --> 07:22.050
H-How long have you noticed?!

07:22.050 --> 07:23.060
From the first.

07:23.060 --> 07:25.010
We can see your face.

07:30.450 --> 07:31.450
Master Fay.

07:31.450 --> 07:34.590
Your battle yesterday
made me think again...

07:34.590 --> 07:36.550
I want to help you!

07:36.990 --> 07:41.930
I beg you! I was defeated by the gods
and can no longer play in the games...

07:41.930 --> 07:44.740
I want to do my best
as an analyst for your team,

07:46.620 --> 07:47.760
Master Fay!

07:48.700 --> 07:49.490
I refuse.

07:50.690 --> 07:52.990
T-Then...!
How about I be your maid?

07:52.990 --> 07:55.580
I'll do all the cleaning, laundry,
and cooking! Everything!

07:55.580 --> 07:56.870
I refuse.

07:59.970 --> 08:01.530
I see...

08:01.530 --> 08:04.060
I'm sorry for wasting your time.

08:04.060 --> 08:06.130
I've made myself too pathetic to bear...

08:06.130 --> 08:08.340
Are you really satisfied with that?

08:09.550 --> 08:15.060
What you really want to do is neither
be an analyst nor a maid, right?

08:16.090 --> 08:18.390
W-What are you talking about, Master Fay?

08:18.390 --> 08:21.230
Tomorrow, we have a meeting
at the Arcane Court.

08:21.770 --> 08:22.610
Huh?

08:27.930 --> 08:30.240
This day has finally come.

08:30.240 --> 08:33.100
Lady Leoleshea, Sir Fay, and Pearl.

08:33.100 --> 08:35.180
Why am I the only one
who doesn't get a title?!

08:35.180 --> 08:37.810
Your real battle is finally here.

08:37.810 --> 08:39.960
It's a battle of wits against the gods.

08:40.330 --> 08:42.040
You currently run a three-person team.

08:42.040 --> 08:44.960
To bring you up to headquarters' recommended
minimum of 10 people,

08:44.960 --> 08:48.400
we have selected 12 apostles
from our branch office.

08:48.400 --> 08:49.680
Thank you very much.

08:49.680 --> 08:50.590
Sure.

08:51.050 --> 08:52.820
They've already dove in.

08:53.690 --> 08:56.900
U-Umm, Chief Secretary?

08:57.390 --> 09:00.230
Why am I here?

09:00.230 --> 09:03.390
Sir Fay told me you'd like
to observe the game.

09:03.390 --> 09:04.140
What?

09:05.100 --> 09:08.980
Master Fay, I spent all last night thinking
about it, but I don't understand.

09:08.980 --> 09:11.440
What was the meaning
of yesterday's conversation?

09:11.440 --> 09:14.300
A teammate is supposed to stay close
and cheer for their teammates.

09:15.200 --> 09:18.040
I know you're unhappy
that all you can do is root for us.

09:18.040 --> 09:20.350
Now you just have to trust
and cheer for us.

09:21.350 --> 09:23.130
What does that mean, Master Fay?

09:23.130 --> 09:25.340
- Now, let's go!
- Ah! Don't push me!

09:25.340 --> 09:27.490
- Ah! Don't push me!

09:27.490 --> 09:28.470
Master Fay!

09:29.050 --> 09:31.420
I still don't know what you're saying,

09:31.420 --> 09:34.250
but since I'm here,
there's only one thing to do:

09:34.930 --> 09:36.970
I will do my best to support you!

09:37.830 --> 09:38.830
Sure!

09:39.980 --> 09:42.980
GODS' GAME WE PLAY
IS IT NOT TIME YET?

09:47.940 --> 09:53.030
Ugh, it's hot! What is this sunshine?

09:54.160 --> 09:56.990
This is a real desert.

09:56.990 --> 09:59.250
What game are we going to play this time?

09:59.790 --> 10:01.480
I've been waiting for you, Fay!

10:06.900 --> 10:09.360
Show me your true worth!

10:09.790 --> 10:11.880
It is a pleasure to be
working with you again.

10:12.370 --> 10:14.930
He was going to make an appearance...

10:20.490 --> 10:23.020
Hello, Lady Dragon God Leoleshea.

10:23.020 --> 10:25.120
And Fay and Pearl.

10:25.120 --> 10:26.100
My name is—

10:26.100 --> 10:27.260
Her name is Camilla.

10:27.260 --> 10:31.360
The others are members of "Archangel,"
the team Camilla is leading.

10:31.360 --> 10:33.270
Hey, why are you saying it?!

10:33.270 --> 10:35.240
They're only here
to make up the numbers.

10:35.240 --> 10:37.180
That's the rudest thing
I've ever heard!

10:38.870 --> 10:40.060
Fay.

10:41.660 --> 10:45.940
This is your event.
It's not my place to interfere with you.

10:45.940 --> 10:49.090
But! I'm looking forward
to your gameplay

10:49.090 --> 10:51.760
as my destiny rival.

10:51.760 --> 10:55.300
Huh? Oh, well, I'll just try
to do what I always do.

10:55.660 --> 10:57.010
Good!

10:57.890 --> 11:00.010
Now the stage is set!

11:00.010 --> 11:01.260
Come forth, O God!

11:01.260 --> 11:03.450
Are you trying to be
the center of attention?!

11:07.630 --> 11:08.940
T-That's...!

11:15.820 --> 11:17.640
W-What is that?

11:18.260 --> 11:19.280
Is that...

11:23.740 --> 11:24.890
...a pyramid?

11:26.060 --> 11:27.730
Hello!

11:27.730 --> 11:30.420
Welcome to my god's Elements!

11:31.540 --> 11:34.000
Oh? 15 participants?

11:34.000 --> 11:37.280
That's a couple digits short
of what my master had in mind.

11:37.280 --> 11:38.760
Eh? What did you just say?

11:38.760 --> 11:42.010
But it's time to start,
so I'll end participation here

11:42.010 --> 11:44.570
and start explaining the game!

11:44.570 --> 11:45.610
Now, now!

11:45.610 --> 11:49.750
I'll give you a flower for each of you
as a sign of friendship!

11:59.200 --> 12:00.570
Hee...

12:00.570 --> 12:03.730
They're buds that are about to be flowers.

12:03.730 --> 12:07.120
You have to take care of it because
if you lose it, you are disqualified.

12:07.120 --> 12:11.000
When those buds bloom, they become
flowers in three different colors.

12:11.000 --> 12:13.850
Each of them is golden, black, and white.

12:13.850 --> 12:15.900
SUN FLOWER
The golden one is the "Sun Flower,"

12:15.900 --> 12:19.120
SUN FLOWER
of which there is only one for each team.

12:19.120 --> 12:20.880
POISON FLOWER
Black is the "Poison Flower," which is

12:20.880 --> 12:23.330
POISON FLOWER
also only one flower for each team.

12:23.330 --> 12:25.810
SAND FLOWER
And white is "Sand Flower."

12:25.810 --> 12:27.100
SAND FLOWER
The remaining 13 flowers

12:27.100 --> 12:28.600
SAND FLOWER
will be this kind of flower.

12:29.140 --> 12:33.910
The goal is to offer the Sun Flower
on the highest level of the pyramid.

12:33.910 --> 12:37.070
The name of this game is
"Sunsteal Scramble"!

12:37.530 --> 12:40.280
The distance is roughly
2-3 kilometers to the pyramid.

12:40.810 --> 12:44.750
That would take me
less than five minutes

12:44.750 --> 12:46.820
if there were no obstacles.

12:46.820 --> 12:49.260
Of course there would be.

12:49.260 --> 12:51.380
It's called a scramble game after all.

12:51.380 --> 12:53.450
As you can see,

12:53.450 --> 12:57.590
my master's team is the defending team
that is trying to steal your flowers.

12:57.590 --> 12:59.420
Let me introduce you.

12:59.420 --> 13:03.300
Come out, the beasts created
by the hand of my master!

13:19.260 --> 13:20.560
Those are cats!

13:23.870 --> 13:25.950
S-So cute!

13:31.140 --> 13:33.130
H-Huh?

13:35.520 --> 13:37.300
They're so huge!

13:37.300 --> 13:40.700
So these cats are the defenders
on god's team, huh?

13:40.700 --> 13:44.330
Yes, they will try to steal your flowers.

13:44.330 --> 13:45.260
On the other hand,

13:45.260 --> 13:47.820
if you all take the flowers
that the beast has,

13:47.820 --> 13:50.100
the beast will leave the field.

13:50.100 --> 13:52.400
And if the Sun Flower is stolen,

13:52.400 --> 13:53.060
your whole team will lose.

13:53.060 --> 13:55.060
DEFEAT
your whole team will lose.

13:55.060 --> 13:58.060
My master's team also has the Sun Flower.

13:58.060 --> 14:02.570
So taking away their flower
is also one of the strategies.

14:02.570 --> 14:04.740
Then, what about the other two flowers?

14:04.740 --> 14:08.230
The Sand Flower is a camouflage,
which does not affect the outcome

14:08.230 --> 14:09.990
of the game whether it is stolen or not.

14:09.990 --> 14:12.970
But if you steal the Poison Flower,

14:12.970 --> 14:15.440
your team will get debuffed.

14:15.440 --> 14:18.100
Not only will they know
who has the Sun Flower,

14:18.100 --> 14:19.250
but everyone on the team

14:19.250 --> 14:21.170
STUN
will be stunned for five seconds.

14:21.610 --> 14:25.890
While you get stunned,
you cannot move, attack, or defend.

14:26.390 --> 14:28.450
This applies to both teams.

14:28.450 --> 14:30.850
It's like letting them steal
from you on purpose, huh?

14:30.850 --> 14:33.860
If we successfully let them
steal the Poison Flower,

14:33.860 --> 14:37.170
can we escape for about
20 meters in five seconds?

14:37.170 --> 14:40.820
A five-second stun means
almost a confirmed defeat.

14:40.820 --> 14:42.150
What?!

14:42.150 --> 14:44.950
If we let Leshea do whatever
she wants for five seconds,

14:44.950 --> 14:46.910
she can take away all the flowers, right?

14:46.910 --> 14:48.890
Ah, that's right...

14:48.890 --> 14:50.860
The conditions are the same for us.

14:50.860 --> 14:54.500
If we take the Poison Flower by mistake,
we will be defeated.

14:54.940 --> 14:58.770
We must protect the Sun Flower
and let them steal the Poison Flower.

14:58.770 --> 15:00.780
It will be a test of acting ability, insight,

15:00.780 --> 15:03.470
and team strategy to see who has the flower.

15:04.300 --> 15:08.390
Is it alright to exchange information
about who has a certain flower?

15:08.390 --> 15:12.850
Of course. You can nudge
open the buds a little.

15:13.760 --> 15:17.020
It's white...
So this is Sand Flower.

15:17.420 --> 15:19.650
My flower is Sun Flower.

15:19.650 --> 15:21.980
Mine is Poison Flower.

15:23.920 --> 15:25.820
The rest is Sand Flower.

15:25.820 --> 15:29.010
You're all aware of
who has which flower now, right?

15:29.010 --> 15:30.830
You're free to swap your flowers!

15:30.830 --> 15:34.160
You must carefully decide
who must carry the flower.

15:35.690 --> 15:41.000
Let's get this straight: Sunsteal Scramble
had three conditions for winning or losing.

15:41.000 --> 15:41.790
WIN CONDITION 1:

15:41.790 --> 15:43.630
RUN TO THE PYRAMID AND PLACE
THE SUN FLOWER ON THE HIGHEST LEVEL

15:43.630 --> 15:44.320
WIN CONDITION 2:

15:44.320 --> 15:45.630
STEAL THE GOD TEAM'S SUN FLOWER

15:45.630 --> 15:46.250
LOSE CONDITION:

15:46.250 --> 15:48.050
THE HUMAN TEAM'S SUN FLOWER IS STOLEN

15:48.050 --> 15:51.430
It was several thousand meters to the pyramid
that loomed on the horizon.

15:51.430 --> 15:53.250
It's a desert race across the desert,

15:53.250 --> 15:56.270
with the god and the cat golems
trying to chase us.

15:56.270 --> 15:57.390
That's right.

15:57.390 --> 15:59.190
Those golems are pretty fast,

15:59.190 --> 16:02.480
so it's important to be
physically fit to escape.

16:02.480 --> 16:06.700
Well, the right person to hold
the Sun Flower is obvious, isn't it?

16:07.860 --> 16:10.000
I don't mind holding it myself.

16:10.000 --> 16:10.910
But...

16:13.610 --> 16:16.120
Wouldn't it be more interesting
if I had the Poison Flower?

16:16.120 --> 16:17.590
I thought so too.

16:17.590 --> 16:19.520
That could be possible.

16:19.520 --> 16:21.500
The god's team would expect

16:21.500 --> 16:24.300
that Leshea is holding the Sun Flower.

16:24.300 --> 16:27.220
So, I think it is a powerful strategy
to use it against them.

16:27.220 --> 16:29.550
Then, who should have the Sun Flower?

16:31.360 --> 16:33.260
A Superhuman would be ideal.

16:34.170 --> 16:36.350
Anyone here fit the bill?

16:41.620 --> 16:42.770
Huh?

16:44.720 --> 16:46.490
What's with that expression?

16:46.490 --> 16:48.990
Is it surprising that I have
a Superhuman Arise?

16:49.760 --> 16:50.880
That's unexpected...

16:50.880 --> 16:53.830
I thought you were a mage...

16:54.240 --> 16:57.270
My Arise is instantly
strengthening my body.

16:57.270 --> 17:00.350
Since I have the power to defend myself,
it is not a bad option

17:00.350 --> 17:02.570
for you to leave it to me.

17:02.570 --> 17:04.170
I'll keep that in mind.

17:05.030 --> 17:06.910
Can we trade flowers
during the game?

17:06.910 --> 17:08.340
It's allowed.

17:08.340 --> 17:12.700
But if a situation occurs during the game
where you're not carrying a flower,

17:12.700 --> 17:16.310
even for a moment, you are considered to
have lost your flower and are disqualified.

17:16.670 --> 17:19.390
For example, what if we try
to throw flowers at each other?

17:19.390 --> 17:20.570
No, you cannot.

17:20.570 --> 17:22.950
That means you're not
carrying flowers for a moment,

17:22.950 --> 17:25.690
and you will be disqualified immediately.

17:25.690 --> 17:26.780
Then, if that is the case,

17:26.780 --> 17:29.710
I will replace the two flowers with my Arise!

17:29.710 --> 17:31.340
Shift Change!

17:32.450 --> 17:33.700
No, you can't.

17:33.700 --> 17:34.870
What?!

17:34.870 --> 17:38.500
That's another disqualification because
you don't have a flower at the moment.

17:39.110 --> 17:42.550
How about a player in a tight spot tossing
their flower to the other players?

17:42.550 --> 17:45.830
That would be permitted.

17:45.830 --> 17:49.460
Of course, the player who loses their flower
will be removed from the game.

17:49.460 --> 17:53.590
What we need is perfect teamwork
by the 15 players.

17:53.590 --> 17:56.290
We all have to defend
the Sun Flower at all costs.

17:56.290 --> 17:57.070
Fay.

18:00.560 --> 18:03.210
You decide who must hold the flowers.

18:03.210 --> 18:05.610
This is a game
between you and the gods.

18:05.610 --> 18:07.790
Dax?! What happened with you?!

18:07.790 --> 18:12.750
Normally, you'll say, "I'm the only one
who can hold the Sun Flower!"

18:12.750 --> 18:14.570
What's going on with you?!

18:16.530 --> 18:18.290
Let's make a bet with me.

18:18.290 --> 18:19.450
Interesting.

18:20.340 --> 18:22.070
I lost a bet.

18:22.690 --> 18:26.170
I'm just genuinely interested
to see how my one and only rival

18:26.170 --> 18:30.130
will fare against the gods.

18:32.000 --> 18:33.470
Well, whatever.

18:36.890 --> 18:39.770
Fay, I've arranged our Arise
for your reference.

18:41.730 --> 18:43.580
Here's a list of my team's stats.

18:43.580 --> 18:46.810
It's a detailed record of our wins,
losses, and our Arise.

18:49.380 --> 18:50.320
Thank you.

18:50.750 --> 18:51.570
I've got it.

18:51.570 --> 18:52.580
Already?!

18:53.470 --> 18:57.210
Now, I want all of you to give your
flowers to me for a minute.

18:57.210 --> 18:59.120
I'll shuffle them.

19:00.790 --> 19:03.410
The one who will hold
Sun Flower and Poison Flower...

19:09.090 --> 19:10.170
I've decided.

19:19.980 --> 19:20.810
Everyone...

19:20.810 --> 19:24.010
I want you to look at your flowers
just like we did before.

19:24.010 --> 19:25.890
But make sure no one
sees what you have.

19:32.320 --> 19:33.900
So it's come to that.

19:35.950 --> 19:38.330
At this point, my strategy begins.

19:38.330 --> 19:40.700
As for exactly what that strategy is...

19:40.700 --> 19:44.910
Wait a minute!
Tell us who has the Sun Flower first!

19:44.910 --> 19:47.630
No, it's key to my strategy.

19:47.630 --> 19:50.140
I'm not telling anyone
where the Sun Flower is.

19:50.140 --> 19:51.040
Say what?!

19:51.040 --> 19:55.550
If I tell you who has it,
you will focus on protecting them.

19:55.550 --> 19:58.260
And then the god will know
where the Sun Flower is, right?

19:58.260 --> 20:01.970
On the other hand, if you don't tell
your allies, god won't know either.

20:01.970 --> 20:03.460
Isn't that right?

20:05.040 --> 20:07.890
The god is already used to this game.
Then...

20:07.890 --> 20:12.230
What we have to challenge is a new strategy
that god has never seen before.

20:12.620 --> 20:14.320
I want you all to trust me!

20:15.600 --> 20:17.850
I guess your plan is set!

20:17.850 --> 20:22.500
Now, let us welcome my master, Mahtma II!

20:33.660 --> 20:34.630
Is it not time yet?

20:35.410 --> 20:36.840
Is it time for the game?

20:38.300 --> 20:41.200
W-What's happening?
He's whispering in my ear!

20:41.200 --> 20:42.580
Telepathy?

20:42.580 --> 20:43.560
U-Um!

20:43.560 --> 20:46.090
I've got a question, Mahtma II!

20:46.090 --> 20:50.160
If you're Mahtma II,
does that mean there's a Mahtma I?

20:51.010 --> 20:51.820
There is not.

20:51.820 --> 20:53.730
That doesn't make any sense!

20:54.960 --> 20:57.310
Everything in this world is just a game.

20:57.310 --> 20:59.280
Including my name.

21:01.020 --> 21:02.240
That's...

21:02.640 --> 21:04.460
So that's god's flower.

21:04.460 --> 21:06.370
You think it's the Flower Sun?

21:06.370 --> 21:10.340
Because it is safe to hold it by himself,
so the possibility is high.

21:10.340 --> 21:13.460
"Go ahead and take it, if you can," huh?

21:15.310 --> 21:19.670
Then I'll make it a game
that'll trick him directly!

21:20.150 --> 21:21.870
The game now begins.

21:21.870 --> 21:26.080
Humans, I urge you to play
with all your wit and all you have.

21:29.500 --> 21:32.350
What are you doing, humans?

21:32.350 --> 21:33.940
Exactly what it looks like.

21:33.940 --> 21:38.010
The game's started, right?
So have we.

21:38.540 --> 21:41.150
The one who holds the Sun Flower...

21:41.630 --> 21:42.530
- ...is me!
- ...is me!

21:49.740 --> 21:50.540
So slow.

21:50.540 --> 21:52.490
They're too slow!

21:52.490 --> 21:55.410
Even they've promised
to play with me again!

21:55.410 --> 21:57.550
Grr, I can't wait any longer!

22:01.090 --> 22:02.210
UNDEFEATED

22:03.210 --> 22:06.220
UNDEFEATED

22:06.650 --> 22:09.530
I'll go looking for you, humans.
